WEBVTT

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.960
The Face-lifter won't come to your dreams again.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.130
Thank you.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:12.300
But more importantly,
I wanted to ask you something.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.550
There were fireworks in your dream a week ago.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.670
Yet they were yesterday's fireworks.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.960
Where <i>is</i> Muku?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.090
She was tired from going
to the firework festival.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.750
She said she'll come at noon.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.920
Well, I'm sure anything can
happen in a dream, but...

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.460
People who will kill me enter my dreams.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:41.380
Those people bring their feelings
and plans about the future with them.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.300
That influences my dreams.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.880
In other words... sometimes your
dreams depict the future.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.630
I can't say whether or not they're accurate,

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.210
but it seems they do sometimes.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:02.340
A potential future...
Is it basically like a premonition?

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.840
It might be something close to that.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.500
I can't really say.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:18.050
I feel like I was in a never-ending dream.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.920
That can't be.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.840
Once I dozed off for just five minutes,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.500
but in that time, the killer slowly and
carefully tore my arms off with his bare hands.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.050
The Arm-twister.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:43.960
Can't the time within a dream be
unrelated to the time outside it?

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:48.090
Detective, what happened in <i>your</i> dream?

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.000
See you tomorrow, Aki.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.750
Good night.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.210
A dream.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:08.750
What if... everything I experienced
up to that point

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:15.300
was one long dream I had inside Ms. Asukai?

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:25.880
It's hard to believe, and I feel like
there are tons of contradictions...

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.300
But that would mean this is reality.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.500
A potential future?

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.170
Premonitions?

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.050
I don't know.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:41.130
Regardless, right now this is where I am,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:46.300
and I at least eliminated the Challenger
and the Face-lifter here.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.750
Which means there's more.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.420
More I can do.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.090
Hello there.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:02.050
Your injuries look much better.

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.800
Thankfully.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.420
What are you up to now?

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.170
Up to? Just spending time with my family.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.420
Who looks so run down from family time?

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.340
It's the truth.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.250
I'm spending time with my family.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.170
Every second I can get.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:25.840
Fine. I won't inquire further
about the Challenger incident,

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.590
and the report's handled.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:30.050
It really was a hunch.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.500
Fine.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.590
Are you visiting Ms. Asukai?

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.630
Yeah. You, too?

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.840
Yes. But it's been a while.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.090
How has she been doing?

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:44.380
She's increasingly frail.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.500
As if the Challenger were still here.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.380
He <i>is</i> .

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.210
Inside her head.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.210
Come in.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.340
Are we interrupting?

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.050
No.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.130
That's enough for today.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.170
Um, excuse me.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:19.050
May I ask your name?

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.500
Shirakoma.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.960
My name is Shirakoma Nishio.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.840
I'm sorry.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.460
It's difficult to even sit up on my own now.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:36.460
It's not a problem. Please, take it easy.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.840
Their hideouts were far away,
so it took a while.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.130
Besides the Face-lifter,
I've eliminated the Tongue-tearer,

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:47.920
the Thigh-severer, and the
Arm-twister from your dreams.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.170
I let them decide for themselves how to end it.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:57.500
Apparently the drive to kill others
turns toward the self when you do that.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:04.090
I suppose by bringing about their own death
with the very method they used on others,

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:07.500
maybe they feel a sense of completion.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:14.590
I interrogated each of them about
our man with the top-hat and cane.

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:17.710
But I didn't learn anything.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:23.130
Ms. Asukai, he appeared alone
in your dreams, correct?

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.630
Yes.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.960
Were there no clues about his identity?

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.460
No.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:35.500
At first you believed he was fictitious. I see.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.920
Yes.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:42.630
I felt how you felt at the time.
That confirms it.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.880
I'm so sorry.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.000
He tormented you in your dreams,

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.550
and before long, other murderers
started appearing, too.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:58.380
Then, agreeing to share their toy,
they killed you, repeatedly.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.420
Forgive me.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.340
I just can't help it.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.250
I'm okay.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:10.420
But you're nowhere close to okay, are you.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:13.590
I see what the memory does to you.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:17.460
Only the man with the cane is left.
I'll have to catch him after all.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.210
He caused everything.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.880
No.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:24.840
As long as I live, the dreams will continue.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:28.840
Even after you've completely
eradicated the killers,

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:37.210
my memories will gradually change
and continue to kill me, over and over.

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:43.250
I can tell that I'm losing myself
in a world of violence.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:47.130
It feels like my self is about to disintegrate.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.300
"Disintegrate"?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:53.300
I will cease to be me.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.880
I don't mean my body will die.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:07:01.710
It's like I'll dissolve and spill out
into the world and combine with it.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:04.170
That's how I'll end.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.670
That's ridic--

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.750
But there's more to it.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:13.420
By blending with it, I'll surely
distort the structure of the world.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:14.880
That's impossible.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.920
I want to die human.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.460
When I said I hoped you'd
put an end to my misery,

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.550
that's what I meant.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.170
I can't do that.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:38.630
You can watch me cruelly slip away
or allow me to have my suffering ended.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:40.300
You can't make that choice?

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.840
I can't.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:43.710
I'm a police officer.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:48.380
In that case, if it's not to save me
but to save the world,

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:51.380
then can I have you eliminate me?

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.210
Ms. Asukai.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:57.090
Please. My dreams have been
telling me it will happen.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:02.340
Very soon, I'll fall apart and warp the world!

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.670
Don't let me, Mr. Narihisago--

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:07.670
The most I can do is
eliminate the serial killers.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:13.670
I'll keep searching for the man with the cane,
but I can't come back here anymore.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:18.090
Ms. Asukai, that man from before...

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:28.380
Hello?

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:30.840
Hey. Sorry for calling so late.

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:34.380
Listen, Ms. Asukai disappeared.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.630
Thirteen nurses have lost consciousness.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:39.130
But there's no sign they were drugged.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:40.500
The cause is unknown.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:41.920
Thirteen?

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:46.210
Three of them have woken up,
but according to their statements,

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.960
they fell into comas in the order
they entered Ms. Asukai's room.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.750
When they came to, Ms. Asukai was gone.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:58.420
The security cameras malfunctioned, too,
so much is unknown.

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:03.500
Narihisago, did Ms. Asukai say
anything to you that might help?

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:08.300
No. I haven't seen her in over a month now.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:12.300
Do you know about Ms. Asukai's dreams?

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:18.420
It seems she always had nightmares.
You remember she was afraid to sleep.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:22.170
No. That's news to me.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:26.210
I see. Well, the dream stuff doesn't end there.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:31.000
The three nurses who woke up
each said they had a strange dream.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.920
And the details all match up.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:37.000
Just as if they'd shared the same dream.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.340
That's certainly strange.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.590
But from what you've told me,

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:44.340
there's a possibility Ms. Asukai
somehow made the nurses faint,

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:47.090
then snuck out of the hospital.

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.920
I visited her two days ago.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:55.090
She was barely conscious.
Hardly in any condition to do that.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.800
Huh. Then I don't have anything for you.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.880
Sorry. Bye.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:06.170
Everything okay?

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:08.090
Yep.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:10.130
No big deal.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:27.130
The world will fall apart.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:32.340
Still investigating Ms. Asukai's whereabouts?

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:33.710
Yeah.

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:36.590
Still no leads, though.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:41.210
But it looks like she had some sort of ability

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:44.300
and had become a subject
of research at the hospital.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:45.880
Research?

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:49.750
"Invasion of the Unconscious
Mediated by Dreams."

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:54.340
It appears to be the independent research
of that Shirakoma guy we met.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.300
So then...

00:10:55.300 --> 00:11:00.460
However, he has an alibi
for the mass coma incident.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:05.000
And he seems not to have had
contact with Ms. Asukai recently.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:10.000
With the speed of her debilitation,
who knows what state she's in.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.340
What is it?

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.420
A visitor.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:24.090
A wanted criminal or something?

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:25.550
No.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.050
The Perforator.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.300
I had forgotten about you.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:44.550
Don't move!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:48.590
Put your pistol on the ground
and slowly turn to face me.

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:58.550
You?

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.300
Narihisago Akihito?

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:01.960
How are you here?

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:07.420
Mr. Narihisago, my name is Hondomachi.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:09.300
I'm a Kura field analyst.

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:10.460
Did you...

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:13.710
...also enter the well within the well?

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.380
Could it be? No!

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.840
This isn't a well within a well!

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:26.420
I knew it. You entered as Sakaido, didn't you?

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:28.380
I don't know any Sakaido!

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.210
I'm Narihisago Akihito.

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.630
This is my life!

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:32.920
I live here!

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.340
What?

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:35.960
This is an id well.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.000
It looks the same as
the real world, but it's fake.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.250
No it's not!

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:44.460
Mr. Narihisago, how long has it been
since you came here?

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:46.460
No! You're wrong! Stop it!

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:50.130
Your pistol... Does that mean
you're an officer right now?

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.750
I said stop it!

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:58.130
Then we'll start with me.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:03.840
I came to this world through
a cockpit I found in your id well.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.210
About 20 minutes ago.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:15.130
What's the date today?

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:18.050
April 20th.

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:19.960
2019.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:36.340
Mr. Narihisago, how long has it been
since you came here?

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:41.710
That can't...

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.750
What's this?

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:02.090
This world! It's falling apart!

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:06.000
The two of us were never supposed to meet here.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.000
The id well can't bear the strain
of the contradiction?

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:14.880
Hello?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.920
It's me, Ayako!

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:17.000
You have to get out!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:17.850
Is Muku there?

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:18.640
Yes?

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.960
Take Muku and run, right now!

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.630
What? Run? Where?

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.170
What's gotten into you?

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:26.340
Who is it?

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:29.050
Your dad. He's talking crazy.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:31.210
He is?

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:33.050
Mr. Narihisago.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.550
Aki.

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:39.130
Where are you right now?

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:42.960
I...

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.670
The real me is...

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.340
...in reality.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:22.210
Where you're gone, and Muku's gone, too.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.000
In reality.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.670
What do you mean?

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.090
Dad?

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.750
Muku.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:34.380
I hate that I can't be there
with you and Mom right now.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:37.420
It kills me.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:39.170
Dad, wait, what?

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:41.050
Are you going away?

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.750
Hey, Dad. Don't die, okay?

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:48.170
Aki, I won't die.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:51.840
I would never leave you and Muku like that.

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:59.590
Am I going somewhere?

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:08.460
What do you mean?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:12.000
You and Mom are the ones who left!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.130
Dad?

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.050
Aki?

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:21.710
Yeah?

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.250
Are you okay?

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:25.710
Yeah.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.090
I am.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:30.590
I'm okay.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:33.420
I'll be fine.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:37.210
You're coming back home, right?

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:39.300
Yeah.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:41.420
I definitely am.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:44.550
I'll absolutely go back.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.170
I'm so sorry, Mr. Narihisago. I didn't...

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:55.500
No.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.250
It's better this way.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:05.920
Do you think we'll die, too,
along with this world?

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:07.500
I wonder.

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:10.500
This situation is a first for me, too.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.380
It's incredibly... pretty, isn't it?

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:17.340
Not just this world, but also its demise.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:19.340
Yeah...

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:21.300
It really is.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:24.340
It is a beautiful world.

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:29.210
Mr. Narihisago, what did you
do here for over a year?

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:32.710
I spent time with my family and did my job.

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:37.630
My job as a police officer,
and a more personal one.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:38.670
Right!

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:42.340
I have to tell you something about John Walker!

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:45.130
Director Momoki?

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.210
No way!

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:49.340
Our only option is to find the real culprit.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:53.880
My body must be left in
the desert, so I'm a goner.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.380
But you still have a chance.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:59.960
Momoki and the others will rescue you.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:04.710
Seems like there's still time
before the well fully collapses.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:10.340
Let's focus on investigating John Walker
in this fictitious world.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:13.170
That's ten minutes.

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.210
Finally.

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:21.590
What? After all this time?

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:22.550
Mr. Narihisago!

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.460
Hondomachi, take this!

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.170
What's this?

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:36.460
Sakaido has returned.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:38.170
Prepare to extract.

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.210
Welcome back.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:43.000
So, how was it?

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.000
Hmm. Good question.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.050
I don't remember.

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:49.920
Are you crying?

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.460
I wonder why.

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:57.000
Hey, what's all this?

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.000
I was bored.

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:01.380
I was counting sand.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.550
You're a strange one.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.960
There never was any "watch thief."

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:33.960
We were each tied to one of
Kaeru's wrists with these, right?

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:35.300
Why'd you remove them?

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.090
What a brilliant detective.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:41.000
Observation certainly <i>is</i> key.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:46.300
I was bored during the ten minutes
I waited for you, so I observed the area.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:48.380
Answer me, Anaido.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:53.000
This was a message to stay near Kaeru.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.670
That's happened before, hasn't it?

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.880
Hey, just listen.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:01.500
I also examined that guy over there.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:07.130
He didn't kill us or Kaeru,
but he didn't help us either.

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:10.840
And in his pocket...

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:13.670
...I found this!

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:14.710
That's...

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.710
When did he find a picture?

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:19.920
<i>You</i> don't know who this is.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:22.550
Right, <i>Sakaido</i> ?

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.710
But <i>I</i> do.

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:26.300
I remember.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:29.170
Everything from before this world.

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:30.460
Know what I think?

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:37.460
Maybe the amnesia function applied
when you enter the well just can't affect me.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:41.090
Because you see, I'm missing
not just part of my face,

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:44.500
but part of my brain as well.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:48.250
And so I also remember
the things you've forgotten.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:54.340
You aren't some brilliant detective
just named "Sakaido."

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:58.000
You're Narihisago Akihito.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:59.960
A former cop...

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:02.250
...and a murderer.

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:07.380
Facial reconstruction completed!

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.300
It matches Narihisago!

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:15.630
So Fukuda Tamotsu entered the well
with his consciousness and memories intact?

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:18.500
He deceived us?

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:19.750
Extract them! Hurry!

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:20.840
I can't!

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:25.960
They're out of sync with us!
The extraction system won't function!

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:28.460
It's the message from the lightning well!

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:31.130
"Stay where Kaeru is."

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:33.130
Sorry.

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:36.340
I knew what this place was.

00:22:36.340 --> 00:22:40.550
Because they had me search for the little lady.

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:46.500
This isn't Mr. Momoki's id well!

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:48.710
It's the end stage of Narihisago's!

00:22:48.710 --> 00:22:51.630
When you remember yourself in your own well,

00:22:51.630 --> 00:22:57.090
to protect the unconscious from the conscious,
the id well whips up a storm!

00:22:57.090 --> 00:22:59.300
He's falling into dogma!

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:02.750
So this is a well storm!

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:06.840
John...

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:08.090
...Walker!
